@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Update count and ring on change
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (UI components)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TodoItemComponent" as item
  participant "TodoPageComponent" as page
  participant "TodoHeaderComponent" as header
  participant "TodoFilterComponent" as filter
end box
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (state and API client)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TodoStore" as store
end box
user -> item : Complete a task (example: 3 active and 2 completed become 2 active and 3 completed)
item -> page : Emit toggled(true)
page -> store : toggle(id, true) updates the todos signal optimistically
store -> store : Recompute activeCount, completedCount (L2-007)
store -> store : Recompute progress, completed divided by total (L2-007)
store --> page : New counts and progress
page -> header : Bind date, activeCount, completedCount
alt Tasks exist and all are completed
  header --> user : Show "All done" instead of a number (L2-007)
else Tasks exist and some are active
  header --> user : Show "n left", for example "2 left" with the ring 60% filled (L2-007)
else No tasks exist
  header --> user : Show "0 left" with an empty ring (L2-007)
end
header -> header : Animate ring to the new value within 300 ms (L2-007)
page -> filter : Bind allCount, activeCount, doneCount from the same signals
filter --> user : Show "All 5", "Active 2", "Done 3" style counts (L2-007)
@enduml
